messages.body_plain:
Dear R users,

Given ten count numbers (1,7,16,13,11,11,12,10,8,4),
I need to test if
(a) the biggest (i.e. 16) and is significantly  higher than other values
(b) the top two values as a group (16 and 13) is significantly  higher than
other values

For question (a), someone told me that log-linear model could do this, and
give me a SAS script like this:

data Count;
input group $ num;
datalines;
A 1
B 7
C 16
D 13
E 11
F 11
G 12
H 10
I 8
J 4
;run;

ods html file="count";
title "log-linear model";
PROC GENMOD DATA=count;
    CLASS Group;
    MODEL num = group/ LINK=LOG DIST=P;
    CONTRAST 'Group 3 Vs. others' group 1 1  -9 1 1 1 1 1 1 1;
RUN;
ods html close;

I'm new to R and statistics, so I really need your help to (1) judge if
this method is good and (2) translate the script to R commends.

Many thanks for any help

Best regards

Hao
